Description: Raise the headphone (cue) gain ceiling for the DDJ-400 on the Pi
 On the XDJ400 (Pi 4B + DDJ-400, raw-ALSA output), the cue bus (ch 3-4)
 tops out far too quiet even with [Master],headGain maxed. A bypass test
 (aplay injecting a -6 dBFS tone straight into hw:CARD,0 ch 3-4, Mixxx out
 of the loop) is loud AND clean, which exonerates the DAC, ALSA, the
 snd-usb-audio driver, the S24_3LE format, and PortAudio: the DDJ-400's
 headphone DAC has ~20 dB of clean headroom above the level Mixxx reaches.
 .
 The bottleneck is Mixxx's single headphone gain stage, whose ceiling is
 +14 dB (linear x5.0 -- the "reaches 5.0" the user saw on screen). The cue
 PFL on this rig lands so low that even +14 dB leaves it quiet while still
 well below 0 dBFS, so the knob "runs out" (plateaus) before the signal is
 loud. Raising the ceiling to +30 dB gives ~16 dB more usable travel; the
 aplay headroom proof means that extra gain lands clean rather than
 clipping. The stage is an audio-taper pot, so unity (0 dB) stays at knob
 centre and only the top end extends -- existing behaviour below unity is
 unchanged.
 .
 Note: if the physical HEADPHONES LEVEL knob is re-mapped to headGain in
 the DDJ-400 MIDI script, scale it to the new max (linear x31.6 = +30 dB)
 or drive it via setParameter, or it will still cap at the old x5.0.
Author: Pioneered CI <pioneered-build@localhost>
Forwarded: no

--- a/src/engine/enginemixer.cpp
+++ b/src/engine/enginemixer.cpp
@@ -125,7 +125,7 @@ EngineMixer::EngineMixer(
             new EngineDelay(ConfigKey(group, "microphoneLatencyCompensation"));

     // Headphone volume
-    m_pHeadGain = new ControlAudioTaperPot(ConfigKey(group, "headGain"), -14, 14, 0.5);
+    m_pHeadGain = new ControlAudioTaperPot(ConfigKey(group, "headGain"), -14, 30, 0.5);

     // Legacy: the headphone "headGain" control used to be named "headVolume" in
     // Mixxx 1.11.0 and earlier. See issue #7413.
